R-CV6 R-CV3 R-CV1 R-CV4 R-CC8 R-TF3 R-EC16 R-EC19 R-SC10 R-C7 R-SO13 R-SO22 R-DL1 (slice 030b): the first sha256 of each compiler asset in compat.db, with the fake Fx. Every list that `Nightlies.list!` reads (live or cached) records the sha256 of the asset of the host for each release, in one read and at most one write. A tag with another recorded sha256 is no candidate (@latest, ranges, names). A command that names the tag stops with exit 16 (`roc install`, `roc default`, `roc use`, the pin of a project). An installed compiler with that tag stays in use. A busy or failed db: the warning of R-CC8, nothing is recorded, the command goes on. The command is `Run.run!` for each line of `fx/commands` (entry `commands`). The comment above each line says what it shows. `fx/db` has the errors of compat.db (the call number counts db_query and db_write over the case). `given/home*/.cache/roc/talon/compat.tsv` has the recorded rows.
Run 1 to 4: a busy read (call 1), a failed read (call 2), a busy read for a tag that changed (call 3: it goes on and installs), a busy read and a download with a wrong listed digest (call 4: exit 16 from R-CV4). Run 5: the read works: 3 changed tags are dropped, @latest is 2026-10-17, 6 new rows in one write (a cached list). Run 6 and 7: an installed compiler with a changed tag: no list, no db call. Run 8 to 12: the tag is named (the id, a prefix, `roc default`, `roc use`, a project pin): exit 16. Run 13 (home2): rank 4 gives the newest unchanged release in the range. Run 14 (home3): a busy write: the warning, the install goes on. Run 15 (home4): a newer format: exit 19. Run 16 (home2): no changed tag is named: the warnings, then the usual failure (exit 2). Run 17 (home5): a cached list (`--offline`) is recorded too: calls 19 and 20. Run 18 (review Q1): an installed changed tag is the base of `@-2`, and the step skips the changed tag 2026-10-16.
The tree diff covers the dirs `home` and `project` only, so the effects in home2 to home4 are in `calls.log`.
